## Commands

- `npm install`: install dependencies
- `npm run dev`: start the API in development mode on http://localhost:3000
- `npm test`: run the test suite
- `npm run lint`: check code style

Run `npm run lint` and `npm test` before considering a change complete.

## Project Structure

- `server.js` — entry point; starts the Express API on port 3000
- `routes/` — one file per resource (`users.js`, `health.js`)
- `db/store.js` — in-memory data helper
- `tests/` — test files

## Code Style

- Follow the existing lint configuration; fix lint errors rather than disabling rules.
- Match the conventions of surrounding code (naming, module style, error handling).
- Keep changes small and focused; avoid unrelated refactors.

## Testing

- Add or update tests alongside any behavior change.
- Run the relevant tests after editing, and the full suite before finishing.

## Notes for Claude

- Do not commit secrets or `.env` files.
- Ask before adding new dependencies.
