# Claude Code Setup Notes

## Project commands

- `npm install`: install dependencies
- `npm run dev`: start the API on http://localhost:3000
- `npm test`: run the sample tests
- `npm run lint`: check code style

## Claude Code basics

- `claude`: start an interactive Claude Code session in the current directory
- `claude --version`: print the installed version
- `/init`: slash command (inside a session) that scans the project and generates `CLAUDE.md`

## Files added

- `CLAUDE.md` (repo root): project context Claude Code reads at the start of every session. Still to fill in: what the API does, the stack, real directory layout, code style specifics (ESM/CJS, JS/TS).
- `.claude/settings.json`: shared project settings, meant to be committed.
  - Allows: `npm install`, `npm run dev`, `npm test`, `npm run lint`
  - Denies reading: `.env`, `.env.*`
- `.claude/settings.local.json`: personal overrides; keep out of git (check `.gitignore`).

## Commit steps

```bash
mkdir -p .claude
mv ~/Downloads/settings.json .claude/settings.json
git add CLAUDE.md .claude/settings.json && git commit -m "Add Claude Code project config (CLAUDE.md, settings.json)"
```

- `.claude/settings.json` must exist before `git add`, or it fails with "pathspec did not match".
- Pasting `git add ... git commit ...` on one line without `&&` or a newline between them will fail.

